# 12. Assumptions

## Purpose

Project assumptions define the conditions and premises accepted as valid for planning and executing the Adaptive Vehicle Intelligence Architecture (AVIA) project unless future evidence demonstrates otherwise.

Documenting assumptions promotes transparency, supports engineering decision-making, and enables future review as the project evolves.

---

## Project Assumptions

### PA-001 — Scientific Validity

The project assumes that established scientific laws and engineering principles provide a reliable foundation for analysis, design, and validation.

---

### PA-002 — Systems Engineering Approach

The project assumes that a structured systems engineering methodology improves the quality, traceability, and maintainability of engineering outcomes.

---

### PA-003 — Repository Integrity

The engineering repository is assumed to remain the authoritative source of approved project knowledge, documentation, and engineering decisions.

---

### PA-004 — Continuous Learning

Engineering understanding is expected to evolve through research, analysis, experimentation, review, and validation. Assumptions may therefore be refined when supported by objective evidence.

---

### PA-005 — Interdisciplinary Integration

The project assumes that effective adaptive vehicle systems require the integration of multiple engineering disciplines, including mechanical, electrical, control, computational, mathematical, and human-system engineering.

---

### PA-006 — Future Technology

The project assumes that future technological developments may provide new implementation opportunities without changing the project's engineering objectives or philosophy.

---

### PA-007 — Controlled Evolution

The project assumes that engineering knowledge, documentation, and system architectures will evolve through governed change while preserving traceability and consistency.

---

## Engineering Perspective

Assumptions are starting points for engineering reasoning rather than permanent truths. As the AVIA project progresses, assumptions shall be periodically reviewed and either confirmed, refined, or replaced based on validated engineering evidence.
